[Retroactive note added later, per the Symptom/Ruled out/Root cause/Fix commit-message framework]

Symptom: number-row hotkeys (1-9, Skill Bar/Hotkey Bar) completely
unresponsive in-game; rebinding one showed "Unspecified value" instead
of registering the keypress.

Ruled out: initially hypothesized a "stuck Alt modifier" left over from
Option-mapped-to-Alt shortcut use (a known Wine Mac-driver bug class) —
disproven by the user's counter-evidence (had not used any Option+letter
combo before the symptom appeared; Option+W/Option+S both worked
correctly for movement). Also directly ruled out Step 9b's Option=Alt
fix itself as the cause via an A/B test: removed the
LeftOptionIsAlt/RightOptionIsAlt registry keys entirely and the symptom
persisted unchanged.

Root cause: the Mac's active keyboard input source was a CJK (Chinese)
input method, which intercepts number-row keys system-wide for
candidate-word selection before Wine or the game ever receives them —
unrelated to Wine, Whisky, or Step 9b entirely.

Fix: documented as a new Known Open Issue with the fix (switch to an
English/ABC input source) and the macOS per-window-input-source-memory
complication. (A live `force-english-input` helper was also built for
the user's own machine per their explicit instruction — intentionally
NOT included in this commit or documented in SKILL.md.)
